  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "33dbd2c03434884269ec64ed27a94cccd1150d1dcc8ccaaa54473592386cbbf4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-33dbd2c03434-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked whether the language of Pennsylvania Public Welfare v. Davenport, which defined a claim as a right to payment and enforceable obligation, controls this case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "33dbd2c03434884269ec64ed27a94cccd1150d1dcc8ccaaa54473592386cbbf4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-33dbd2c03434-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor followed up by asking whether a breach of the trustee\u2019s duties occurs when the trustee fails to object to a claim."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "33dbd2c03434884269ec64ed27a94cccd1150d1dcc8ccaaa54473592386cbbf4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-33dbd2c03434-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito questioned why time\u2011barred claims slip through and why trustees do not automatically object to them."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "33dbd2c03434884269ec64ed27a94cccd1150d1dcc8ccaaa54473592386cbbf4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-33dbd2c03434-0001-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan asked whether any affirmative defenses, particularly bankruptcy\u2011related ones, might apply to the arguments presented."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "33dbd2c03434884269ec64ed27a94cccd1150d1dcc8ccaaa54473592386cbbf4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-33dbd2c03434-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 43,
              "start": 43
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer inquired whether the record shows that the debt\u2011collector\u2019s business model is to buy worthless debts and file suits hoping they go unnoticed."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Oral Argument",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Geyser",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "33dbd2c03434884269ec64ed27a94cccd1150d1dcc8ccaaa54473592386cbbf4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-33dbd2c03434-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Geyser, midland Funding, LLC (petitioner) argues that debt collectors must have a good\u2011faith belief that a claim is enforceable before filing a proof of claim in bankruptcy."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Geyser",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "33dbd2c03434884269ec64ed27a94cccd1150d1dcc8ccaaa54473592386cbbf4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-33dbd2c03434-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Geyser, midland Funding also argues that the cost of objecting to a time\u2011barred claim often exceeds the benefit, leading trustees to refrain from objection."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Geyser",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "33dbd2c03434884269ec64ed27a94cccd1150d1dcc8ccaaa54473592386cbbf4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-33dbd2c03434-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Geyser, the petitioner further notes that trustees face information asymmetry and may assume creditors act in good faith, which can cause time\u2011barred claims to go unchallenged."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Sarah E. Harrington",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "33dbd2c03434884269ec64ed27a94cccd1150d1dcc8ccaaa54473592386cbbf4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-33dbd2c03434-0002-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Sarah E. Harrington, aleida Johnson (respondent), supported by an amicus brief, argues that no creditor may file a time\u2011barred claim in bankruptcy and that such claims should be disallowed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Harrington",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "33dbd2c03434884269ec64ed27a94cccd1150d1dcc8ccaaa54473592386cbbf4",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-33dbd2c03434-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 56,
              "start": 56
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Ms. Harrington, the respondent\u2019s position is that, if the bankruptcy system works as Congress intended, 100\u202f% of time\u2011barred claims should be disallowed."
      }
    ],
